  "description": "Result, Result<T> and Result<T, TError> for returning expected failures instead of throwing, with typed errors: each failure is a record carrying its own data, described by an [Error] attribute (code, status, message), and an operation declares the errors it returns as a C# 15 union, so callers switch over them exhaustively and documentation lists each one with its data. A source generator lists every error and error set at build time and reports duplicates and undeclared errors as build errors. No dependencies. Pair it with Hlibz.Results.AspNetCore to turn results into HTTP responses.",
